System V semaphore operations and named semaphores (ADR 0490). semop
and semtimedop go to a new sysdep, Semtimedop, in place of patch 0037's
ENOSYS; <sys/sem.h> declares semtimedop with _GNU_SOURCE, and Linux's
GETNCNT, GETZCNT, SEM_STAT, SEM_INFO, SEM_STAT_ANY and struct seminfo
join the Linux ABI's <abi-bits/sem.h>, where libc-test's ipc_sem needs
them.

sem_open, sem_close and sem_unlink are musl's (1.2.5): a semaphore named
/NAME is the file /dev/shm/sem.NAME (glibc's name for it), made whole
under a temporary name and linked to its own, holding one sem_t that
each process maps shared. A process maps a semaphore once however often
it opens it, and unmaps it when it has closed it as often. Meant for
upstream.

